   163→                // Only trigger payload invalidation in fork choice if the
   164→                // `latest_valid_hash` is `Some` and non-zero.
   165→                //
   166→                // A `None` latest valid hash indicates that the EE was unable
   167→                // to determine the most recent valid ancestor. Since `block`
   168→                // has not yet been applied to fork choice, there's nothing to
   169→                // invalidate.
   170→                //
   171→                // An all-zeros payload indicates that an EIP-3675 check has
   172→                // failed regarding the validity of the terminal block. Rather
   173→                // than iterating back in the chain to find the terminal block
   174→                // and invalidating that, we simply reject this block without
   175→                // invalidating anything else.
